{"schema_version":1,"guid":"6a9a6ce4a0210c197dcd64dc","apple_collection_id":"1559695855","show":"知行小酒馆","titel":"E250 为什么学了这么多知识，却还是做不好投资？","audio":{"url":"https://dts-api.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/track/6013f9f58e2f7ee375cf4216/6a9a6ce4a0210c197dcd64dc/media.xyzcdn.net/6013f9f58e2f7ee375cf4216/lqB8zb64T2Lk_Xh-KdaZQ8hnlGhQ.m4a","user_agent":"PodcastsAM/1.0 (+https://amapps.app)","groesse":97744677,"format":"m4a","geprueft_am":"2026-10-05T12:06:20+00:00"},"faehigkeiten":{"clips":false,"clips_aac":true,"clips_suche":false,"range":true,"kapitel":true,"dynamik":"unbestimmt","grund":"Dynamik weder belegt noch ausgeschlossen (Last-Modified liegt nur 129 s vor dem Abruf) - zu wenig fuer ein Urteil, aber nicht nichts; M4A: Ausschnitte nur als AAC-Bloecke (clips_aac) - eine App ohne ADTS-Umverpackung zeigt keine"},"einzeiler":"Why knowledge does not guarantee successful investing and how coaching changes behavior.","kurzfassung":"Despite knowing numerous investment rules, many individuals struggle to achieve good financial returns due to psychological barriers and a lack of proper discipline. Investment coach Shirley shares her one-on-one coaching approach, explaining how treating investing as a long-term lifestyle rather than a get-rich-quick scheme helps build reliable personal systems. The conversation highlights how mindset, self-awareness, and emotional stability matter far more than mere intellectual understanding or financial background.","stichpunkte":["An investment coach works similarly to a fitness trainer, providing customized, one-on-one guidance rather than generic courses or financial planning.","Shirley transitioned from a 20-year career in finance to personal investing in 2014 to escape the burnout of a job she did not truly believe in.","Analyzing top global wealth rankings reveals that accumulating wealth through industrial business is far more probable than through investing alone.","Most people fail at investing because they treat it like a lottery ticket without building a systematic framework or understanding their true risk tolerance.","Value investing and broad-based ETFs suit everyday individuals best, while short-term trading and macro-hedging demand rare talent and constant screen-watching.","Surviving the first market cycle is the hardest part, requiring investors to convert logical principles into emotional resilience through journaling and clear rules.","True financial freedom is not about stopping work altogether, but about gaining the autonomy to choose tasks aligned with one's genuine passions."],"kapitel":[{"titel":"Introduction to Investment Coaching","start":4.68},{"titel":"Shirley's Career Shift and 2014 Market Entry","start":363.44},{"titel":"Why Most People Fail at Investing","start":1305.2},{"titel":"Selecting Investment Strategies and Value Investing","start":1702.04},{"titel":"Navigating Bear Markets and Developing a System","start":2322.68},{"titel":"Individual Stocks versus ETFs","start":3330.7},{"titel":"The Personal Nature of Coaching and Financial Goals","start":3912.46},{"titel":"Time, Compounding, and True Freedom","start":5462.92}],"clips":[{"hook":"Can an investment coach bridge the gap from knowing to doing?","start":87.339,"ende":107.435,"laenge":20.1,"byte_start":2531615,"byte_ende":2853058,"bytes":321444,"range_header":"bytes=2531615-2853058","vorlauf_s":0.064,"inhalt_start":87.403,"anker_sha256":"5f03ce16313d23197d82961083915326f836a48008a46f9caa0db6a875ee6a20","anker_ende_sha256":"7d9268e363e3cb54ffb68f19b2e597be8fa09bcc535a5cf55454f7359dcf07b7","einblendung_ms":60,"text":"The hosts discuss whether a personalized, long-term companion model serves as the ultimate solution to help investors translate theoretical knowledge into actual behavioral change.","aac":{"profil":2,"samplerate_index":3,"kanaele":1,"bloecke":[323,314,315,322,351,324,336,320,327,332,354,354,350,318,337,320,341,341,342,406,422,356,304,304,331,356,340,336,410,395,298,311,345,395,294,330,335,316,387,304,305,338,328,421,31